      "message": "I would reorganize this function a little bit. It has signs of how it evolved.\n\nThe switchcap whacking is an exceptional case, maybe the rv condition checking should look for an error instead of a success, same for the reason \u003d\u003d CHIPSET_RESET_HOST_CMD.\n\nPerhaps:\n\nif (reason \u003d\u003d CHIPSET_RESET_HOST_CMD)\n    goto cold_reset; // Host really wanted a cold_reset, don\u0027t even try asking the pmic for a nice reset.\n\n// Ask the pmic nicely, Hope the pmic register was programmed for this functionality\ngpio_set_level(GPIO_PM845_RESIN_L, 0);\nusleep(PMIC_RESET_TOGGLE_WAIT);\ngpio_set_level(GPIO_PM845_RESIN_L, 1);\n\nrv \u003d power_wait_signals_timeout....;\nif (!rv) { // pmic was not programmed yet, so it didn\u0027t listen\ncold_reset:\n    // force the ap to reset by power cycling everything\n    power_request \u003d POWER_REQ_RESET;\n    task_wake(TASK_ID_CHIPSET);\n}",
